# The Skia customization patch is consumed byte-for-byte by `patch`, and its added
# lines carry CRLF (they reproduce files that are CRLF in the tree dui builds). Git
# normalizing line endings -- core.autocrlf defaults to true in Git for Windows --
# would append a CR to every line of the patch, including the hunk headers, which
# breaks both the syntax and the CRLF it is supposed to restore.
third_party/skia-patches/*.patch -text
